'''Yagluth''' is the fifth [[Creatures#Bosses|boss]]. He appears as an ancient [[Fuling]] spirit inhabiting a now decomposed skeletal body comprised of a head, two arms and a torso. The crown resting upon his skull implies he was once or still is a ruler of some sort.

== Summoning ==
[[File:YagluthAltar.png|left|thumb|200x200px|Yagluth's Forsaken Altar.]]
Yagluth's [[Forsaken Altars|Forsaken Altar]] is located in the [[Plains]]. His location can be found when visiting [[Stonehenge]] structures, where a [[Runestone#Vegvisir|Vegvisir]] will reveal his nearest summoning location on the map.

He is summoned by placing five {{Item Link|Fuling Totem}}s in his Forsaken Altar in the Plains. Like all [[Creatures#Bosses|bosses]], Yagluth can be summoned as many times as desired, provided the required materials are met.

Yagluth's [[Runestone#Vegvisir|Vegvisir]] has a very small chance of spawning, making it very hard to find. Oftentimes, it is easier to directly find the [[Forsaken Altars|Forsaken Altar]] than the Vegvisir.

== Attacks and abilities ==
{{For|strategies for defeating Yagluth|Boss strategies#Yagluth}}
Yagluth has an environment aura that forces darkness and removes raining, which means [[Wet Effect|Wet]] from rain cannot be used as Fire resistance.

=== Beam ===
Yagluth is able to breathe fire in a roughly 40-meter straight line every 15 seconds, slowly rotating to aim at the player if they are moving. This breath is made up of 20 individual projectiles, each dealing 40 [[Damage types#Fire|Fire]], 20 [[Damage types#Lightning|Lightning]], 50 Tier 1 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 50 Tier 1 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage<ref  group="Note">In the game files, Yagluth is listed as doing Tier 2 and Tier 3 (Beam) damage. For unknown reasons he does not actually behave like this in-game.</ref> and inflicting the [[Burning]] and [[Lightning (effect)|Lightning]] statuses. Each projectile travels at 40 meters per second and can travel for 3 seconds before disappearing. This ability can be used when a player is within 10–40 meters of Yagluth and does not have any spread: meaning he is perfectly accurate.

=== Meteors ===
Every 25 seconds, Yagluth can raise his left fist which glows red. A few seconds later, a volley of 10 burning stones will fall from above and create 5-meter radius explosions wherever they land. Anyone hit is inflicted with [[Burning]] and takes 40 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], 120 [[Damage types#Fire|Fire]], 50 Tier 1 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 50 Tier 1 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage. The meteors fall from the sky 30 meters behind Yagluth and 50 meters off of the ground in a 15-meter radius sphere. They fall at an initial velocity of 30 meters per second and can travel for up to 8 seconds before despawning. This attack can be used when a player is within 30 meters of Yagluth.

=== Nova ===
Yagluth raises his right fist which glows blue before slamming the ground, creating a 10-meter radius spherical explosion beginning at the center of his fist and slowly expanding out to the full radius. Anyone standing within the explosion will be inflicted with the [[Burning]] and [[Lightning (effect)|Lightning]] status and take 65 [[Damage types#Fire|Fire]], 65 [[Damage types#Lightning|Lightning]], 100 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 100 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage. Blue fire will remain in the area for a short time, dealing 100 Fire damage over time. The initial explosion is both dodgeable and blockable, but the lingering fire is not blockable. This ability has a 20-second cooldown and can only be used when a player is within 10 meters of Yagluth.

